-- A TYPICALLY default that is a named call with SEVERAL arguments (W7, R8 rule 3).
-- Its text is written out where a module is generated (`l4 batch`'s wrapper) and
-- published (the schema's `default`), and the printer used to put each argument
-- on a line of its own, which does not survive being spliced after a prefix: the
-- second argument no longer lines up and the parse fails at it. It is now one
-- line, comma-separated, with a bracket round an argument that has an open tail
-- of its own.

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
combine MEANS a PLUS b

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
pair MEANS x TIMES y

§ `Pricing`
    GIVEN `list price` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 200
          discount IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (combine WITH a IS `list price`, b IS 1)
          nested IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (combine WITH a IS (pair WITH x IS 2, y IS 3), b IS discount)

GIVETH A NUMBER
net MEANS discount MINUS `list price`

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (combine WITH a IS 2, b IS 3)
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
rated MEANS rate TIMES base

#ASSERT discount EQUALS 201
#ASSERT nested EQUALS 207
-- 11 less 10: it is 1 only if the default saw the 10 the WITH gave
#ASSERT (net WITH `list price` IS 10) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (rated WITH base IS 10) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT (rated WITH base IS 10, rate IS 1) EQUALS 10
